<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Red River War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1874–1875</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Red River War of 1874–1875 was a campaign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Army against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a>, Kiowa, Southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheyenne">Cheyenne</a> and Arapaho on the southern Plains, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> Panhandle. It began after attacks provoked by the destruction of the bison herds, and columns of troops destroyed camps and horse herds, notably at Palo Duro Canyon. It ended free life on the southern Plains.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/red-river-war.jpg" alt="Red River War" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ledger-sm2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
